{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"blowzy-epicentral-dowitcher","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context / Problem\nThe edit-then-re-review loop is common and hazardous as two shell commands (the review must follow the edit; field incidents lost attestations to mis-sequencing), and claim's recovery text (src/rebar/_commands/gates.py:213-215) tells the user to run review-plan then claim by hand. Operator approved both flags. OSS precedent favors embedding prerequisite verification in the consuming verb (cargo publish verifies by default; terraform apply consumes a staleness-checked plan artifact) over new fused commands.\n\n## Approach\n(1) `rebar edit <id> ... --review`: in edit_cli (src/rebar/_commands/composer.py:506-573), accept `--review` as a non-field flag; after edit_core commits the EDIT event, invoke rebar.llm.review_plan(ticket_id, sign=True) in the foreground and pass through its exit code (0 PASS / 1 BLOCK / 2 INDETERMINATE / 11 retryable). (2) `rebar claim <id> --review`: at the precheck call (src/rebar/_commands/claim.py:133), on a plan-review CommandError run review_plan(sign=True), then re-run plan_review_precheck and proceed on success; the flag is NOT propagated through the parent-first cascade (a surprise multi-minute parent review is a bad default). Both flags are CLI-only (the MCP surface keeps its REBAR_MCP_ALLOW_LLM fence) and their help text states they are not atomic against concurrent store reconvergence, pointing at `review-plan --status` as the cheap currency probe. Alternative rejected: new fused verbs (edit-review/claim-review) — no OSS precedent, larger surface.\n\n## Scope\nsrc/rebar/_commands/composer.py, src/rebar/_commands/claim.py, src/rebar/_cli/__init__.py (help), tests/commands/test_review_flags.py, docs/cli-reference.md.\n\n## Testing\nUnit with a stubbed review_plan: edit --review runs review after the EDIT commit and propagates exit codes; a BLOCK leaves the edit committed and exits 1; claim --review reviews then claims on PASS, fails closed with the standard message when the post-review recheck still fails; the parent cascade never receives the flag.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] edit --review runs the plan review strictly after the EDIT event is committed and propagates the review exit code (checked: unit test with stubbed review_plan recording call order).\n- [ ] claim --review runs review-plan only when the precheck fails, then re-checks and claims on PASS (checked: unit test).\n- [ ] The parent-first cascade does not inherit --review (checked: unit test claiming a child with an open parent).\n- [ ] Both help texts document non-atomicity and reference review-plan --status (checked: help-output test).","id":"a114-8f96-ff2d-461d","parent_id":"a492-3e46-ca44-40a5","priority":2,"tags":[],"ticket_type":"story","title":"edit --review and claim --review flags"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1785384352183857001,"uuid":"c72914ad-d6ab-41d1-8bf1-44d678a0a57f"}